From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] luci-ssl-openssl: do not install package management
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

This downstream target has no compatible binary package repository. Keep HTTPS
LuCI without presenting a package manager whose generated feeds are invalid and
whose packages could be ABI-incompatible with the Qualcomm/TIP stack.

--- a/collections/luci-ssl-openssl/Makefile
+++ b/collections/luci-ssl-openssl/Makefile
@@ -16,8 +16,7 @@ LUCI_DESCRIPTION:=LuCI with OpenSSL as the SSL backend (libustream-openssl). \
 
 LUCI_DEPENDS:=+luci-light \
 	+libustream-openssl \
-	+openssl-util \
-	+luci-app-package-manager
+	+openssl-util
 
 PKG_LICENSE:=Apache-2.0
 
